    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><strong>Tier 3 — Kabbalist</strong></p><p><strong>“Qliphoth lies, but it lies in consistent ways.”</strong></p><p>At Tier 3, you can read the Shells like weather. You are not immune to corruption. You are simply harder to fool.</p><p><strong>Tactical (Character Scale)</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Ritual Literacy:</strong> you reroll the lowest die on Mind (Faith) checks to understand the Lore, weaknesses, bindings, and rituals of Qliphothic entities.</li></ul><p><strong>Strategic (Faction Scale)</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Read the Rot:</strong> once per Scenario involving Qliphothic forces or corrupted Hex conditions, gain <strong>Advantage</strong> on one relevant Strategic Roll, chosen when you roll.</li></ul><p><strong>Cost:</strong> pattern-recognition cuts both ways. Repeated exposure to the Shells can normalize ugliness, invite obsession, or tempt you into treating corruption as merely another readable system.</p><div data-ft-per-use=\"1\" data-ft-per-use-key=\"kabT3\" style=\"margin-top:0.7rem;padding:0.55rem 0.75rem;border:1px solid #b08acc;border-radius:0.35rem;background:rgba(70,55,95,0.18);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.78rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#d4b8e8;margin-bottom:0.25rem\">⟁ Per-Use Ability — <strong>Read the Rot</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.86rem;opacity:0.92;line-height:1.4\"><strong>Recovery:</strong> 1/Scenario &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Action:</strong> Strategic &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Use:</strong> Click this feature on your sheet to invoke.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.82rem;opacity:0.85;margin-top:0.3rem\">In a Scenario involving Qliphothic forces or corrupted Hex conditions, reroll the lowest die on one relevant Strategic Roll.</div>\n</div>",
      "chat": ""
    },
